WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.100
Millions of women are exploring what&nbsp;
it means to transition to natural hair.&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.260
We know that when Black women embrace&nbsp;their love for their natural hair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:16.620
it helps to undo generations of teaching that&nbsp;Black in its natural state is not beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.042
or something to be hidden or covered up.

00:00:20.042 --> 00:00:23.099
Black women express their individuality

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:26.199
and experience&nbsp;feelings of empowerment

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:30.447
by experimenting
with different hairstyles regularly.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:34.221
When we're invited to wear our 
natural hair in the workplace,

00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:37.751
it reinforces&nbsp;that we are uniquely valued.

00:00:37.751 --> 00:00:43.371
So when you see a woman with braids 
or locks draping down her back,

00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:49.513
or you&nbsp;notice your colleague who has stopped straightening her hair to work,

00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:51.603
really appreciate her.

00:00:51.603 --> 00:00:54.534
This is more than about&nbsp;a hairstyle.

00:00:55.439 --> 00:00:58.767
It's about self-love and self-worth.

